            <ArticleTitle>Chronic post traumatic thoracic aortic aneurysm mimicking a benign cyst.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>59-63</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Aneurysm of thoracic aorta may mimic cystic lesions like bronchogenic cyst or hydatid cyst. We report a case of chronic post traumatic thoracic aortic aneurysm in a young lady, initially diagnosed as benign cystic lesion. MRI scan of chest confirmed the diagnosis and subsequently surgical removal of aneurysm was done.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
